  "action": "Fixed two rendering bugs. Bug 1 (citation beads empty): rewrote parseAnswerText in api.ts — changed from stripping PMID numbers out of text and replacing with ref-number beads, to matching complete (PMID: X)/(PMIDs: X,Y)/(PMID: X, PMID: Y) groups as pmid-group segments that preserve the full original text with PMID numbers visible. PMID groups now render as clickable ember-colored underlined spans showing the full text (e.g. '(PMID: 30561177)'), with click handler opening the citation drawer. Regex: /\\(PMID[s]?: \\d{6,9}(?:, (?:PMID: )?\\d{6,9})*\\)/g matches all three formats. Bug 2 (raw markdown): added **bold**→<strong> rendering via regex in renderSegment function (answer/content.tsx) and markdown stripping for card summaries (ask/content.tsx). Verified with node tests on all PMID formats and bold markers. Build passes clean — 7 routes, exit 0. Zero design/visual changes."
